  This shader is PUBLIC DOMAIN as stated in its header:
  "PUBLIC DOMAIN CRT STYLED SCAN-LINE SHADER by Timothy Lottes
   — Please take and use, change, or whatever."

  Files in this directory covered by this notice:
    - crt-lottes.glsl  (vendored single-file original from
        https://raw.githubusercontent.com/libretro/glsl-shaders/master/crt/shaders/crt-lottes.glsl)
    - crt-lottes.vert  (GL 3.3 core split/adaptation for glow)
    - crt-lottes.frag  (GL 3.3 core split/adaptation for glow)
  All three are PUBLIC DOMAIN — no copyright, no license conditions.
  See the header in each file for the Timothy Lottes notice.

  The CPU fallback implementation (src/crt_pi.rs + SDL2 path in src/render.rs)
  is a separate MIT-licensed implementation (© 2026 batk0) that approximates
  similar CRT effects (scanlines, curvature, bloom) for the SDL2 renderer.
  It is not derived from crt-lottes and remains MIT (see root LICENSE).

